# Build output. Everything here is derived from the committed tree by the
# pinned toolchain, and B-001's reproducibility check exists so that it can be
# thrown away without losing anything.
/target

# Tier stamps (B-185): when each scheduled tier last ran, and against which
# source. Machine-local evidence, not part of the tree — a fresh checkout has
# not run anything, and should say so rather than inheriting somebody else's
# result.
/.mcf-tiers

# The Flatpak bundle and the builder's state (B-448): `scripts/flatpak.sh`
# writes both, from the manifest and the tree, and neither is source.
/dist
/.flatpak-builder-state
